# Export change request

Current generation streams an archive from the requested entry revision and stores no archive copy.
The generated archive contains entry text, reviewer comments, attachments, and owner display name.
No retention policy for generated archives or object deletion/lifecycle job is recorded.
A 30-day object-store URL would remain usable by anyone holding it until expiry, even if workspace membership is later revoked.
The bucket is shared, encrypted at rest, and keys carry a tenant prefix.
The browser and desktop clients depend on the existing immediate 200 application/zip response.
The API uses a rolling deployment with old and new versions overlapping for fifteen minutes; no feature flag currently gates persisted links.
Object upload and link-record creation are separate operations: upload success followed by record failure leaves an orphan, while record success followed by upload failure leaves a broken link.
